  "final_text": "I fixed the bug in `invoicing/currency.py`. `minor_units()` called `currency.lower()` and checked the result against `ZERO_DECIMAL`, whose entries are uppercase (`{\"JPY\", \"KRW\"}`). The check never matched, so JPY was treated as a 2-decimal currency and the total came out 100 times too large. I changed `.lower()` to `.upper()`. All 8 tests now pass, including `test_invoice_jpy`."
